// Monochrome icons as SVG path data (24x24 viewbox), rendered with Slint's
// Path element. Material Symbols, outlined — Google's current line, and the
// vocabulary this file's names already came from, so each one is the glyph the
// screen was designed around rather than a near-equivalent from elsewhere.
// A few glyphs ship only one drawing, and take that. Play, pause, next and previous
// take the filled one on purpose: a solid triangle reads as a button to press,
// which is the convention every transport bar follows. Pause is in that
// list because it is the play button's other state, not a separate control.
//
// Filled shapes, not stroked: the outlined look is drawn into the path itself.
// The fill rule has to be even-odd — several of these glyphs cut their holes
// with subpaths wound the same way as the shape around them, which the non-zero
// rule fills solid. The subtitle glyph is the visible one: it came out as a
// featureless white block.
//
// `fill: currentColor` is emulated by the `color` property each call site sets.
export component AppIcon {
    in property <string> data;
    in property <brush> color: white;
    in property <length> size: 24px;
    // Rounds the corners by half this width, by stroking the shape's own
    // outline with a round join. Material's own Rounded style was the obvious
    // route and overshot — it turns the pause bars into full pills — where the
    // transport controls wanted their corners taken off, not redrawn.
    //
    // It has a ceiling, because the stroke also grows the shape outwards by half
    // its width: past about 2px at a 20px icon the negative space goes. Measured
    // at that size, the gap between the pause bars closes and the skip triangle
    // meets its bar. 2px is the most this technique gives before the glyph does.
    in property <length> soften;
    width: size;
    height: size;
    Path {
        commands: root.data;
        fill: root.color;
        stroke: root.soften > 0 ? root.color : transparent;
        stroke-width: root.soften;
        stroke-line-join: round;
        fill-rule: evenodd;
        viewbox-width: 24;
        viewbox-height: 24;
        width: 100%;
        height: 100%;
    }
}

